{"id":"southwark-cathedral","name":"Southwark Cathedral","qid":"Q922967","country":"United Kingdom","locality":"London Borough of Southwark","lat":"51.506111111","lon":"-0.089722222","built":"1150","year":1150,"year_text":"1150","century":"12th century","era":"Middle Ages","period":"","date_basis":"Wikidata, inception","style":"Gothic architecture","heritage":"Grade I listed building","type":"Anglican or Episcopal cathedral","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwark_Cathedral","text":"Southwark Cathedral ( SUDH-ərk), formally the Cathedral and Collegiate Church of St Saviour and St Mary Overie, is a Church of England cathedral in Southwark, London, near the south bank of the River Thames and close to London Bridge. It is the mother church of the Diocese of Southwark. It has been a place of Christian worship for more than 1,000 years, but the church was not raised to cathedral status until the creation of the diocese of Southwark in 1905.","text_source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southwark_Cathedral","text_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","real":[{"id":"gh-7d187de53136","w":1200,"h":901,"title":"Northwest View of Southwark Cathedral (01).jpg","o":"gh-7d187de53136.jpg","credit":{"text":"Ethan Doyle White","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Northwest_View_of_Southwark_Cathedral_%2801%29.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-8c4f640ec3c8","w":1200,"h":900,"title":"Southwark Cathedral at night.jpg","o":"gh-8c4f640ec3c8.jpg","credit":{"text":"Carlos Delgado","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Southwark_Cathedral_at_night.jpg","via":"Wikimedia Commons"}},{"id":"gh-b1ea074fc671","w":1200,"h":800,"title":"Interior, Southwark Cathedral.jpg","o":"gh-b1ea074fc671.jpg","credit":{"text":"Manisha Mishra","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","license_url":"https://creativecommons.